From bb4bc99d7055166647a4e9fa6f41e2151154e7b7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Bulashev <d.bulashev@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 09:46:58 +0500
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] pathprobe: report startup cost, rows, index and
 required_outer in JSON

With path_id and paths[] a consumer can build the path graph, but the
nodes carried only type and relation.  Four facts that decide or
explain a planner choice were missing: the startup cost (a path more
expensive in total can displace another on startup), the row estimate,
the index an index path scans (ambiguous once a table has several),
and the rels a parameterized path depends on (only a boolean so far).

Costs stay on events, and cost_startup joins cost_total.  Rows,
required_outer and the index are properties of a Path that do not
change after it is built, so they go on its paths[] node and are read
when the node is registered, while the Path is live.  SKIPPED events
have no Path; the precheck hook passes required_outer, which is
interned (the caller frees it after the hook) and emitted on the
event.

The index name is looked up at render time.  A pathprobe hypothetical
index has a fake oid from 0x7FFF0000 up, without a catalog entry, and
the number may be a real relation's oid after oid wraparound, so the
node records IndexOptInfo.hypothetical and reports
"index_hypothetical": true instead of an oid and a name; its events
keep the hypo:<name> label.

pathprobe_graph checks the new fields structurally: the inner index
paths name an index of gr_o (gr_o_customer_idx among them), index_oid
and index agree, other paths have none, required_outer is the other
rel and matches the param flag, rows are positive, startup does not
exceed total; and a hypothetical index path reports neither oid nor
name but carries its label.  No cost or row values are asserted.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
